WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.030
A snake!

3
00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:55.870
Wait just a minute.

4
00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.120
Hey! Kalgara! Look at this!

5
00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.120
What a shock.

6
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.330
I didn't realize that
snake had a grandchild.

7
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.440
"That snake," huh?

8
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.800
A snake!

9
00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.780
– Huh?
– Huh?

10
00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.040
Would you look at that?

11
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.910
It doesn't make any sense.

12
00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.750
Those two were trying' to kill
each other not too long ago.

13
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.790
Now they're laughing
together like good friends.

14
00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.300
Usually Kalgara isn't very
friendly with the villagers either.

15
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.750
I've never seen
him smile like that before.

16
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.970
All right, follow me.

17
00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.130
We climb down here.

18
00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.260
Climb down?

19
00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:43.690
<b>The Light of Shandora</b>

20
00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.530
That... ringing.

21
00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.300
Kalgara.

22
00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.060
Where is that beautiful
ringing coming from?

23
00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.970
Follow me and I will show you.

24
00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.770
They're here!

25
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.160
You're speechless. I'm not surprised.

26
00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.540
This is Shandora.

27
00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.260
And we're the survivors
of this golden city.

28
00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.370
A city of gold.

29
00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.880
It's like I'm dreaming!

30
00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.800
It's a city... full of treasure!

31
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.850
There's gold everywhere!

32
00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.440
Hey!

33
00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.850
Wait! Everyone stop!

34
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.140
It's all right.

35
00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.730
Load up your ship with
all the treasure you can.

36
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.800
Just leave the golden bell.

37
00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.680
All the villagers here
agree that this is right.

38
00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.850
It is a gift.

39
00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.800
We want to thank you for saving our
tribe from that terrible disease.

40
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.300
– This is nothing at all.

41
00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.880
You're so generous, Great Warrior!

42
00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.220
But... I don't understand.

43
00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.160
Haven't your people been working
hard to protect this city?

44
00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.280
That's true.

45
00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.830
We have worked hard to protect it.

46
00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.330
Although...

47
00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.330
It's not necessarily
the treasure we guard.

48
00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.080
Come!

49
00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.370
Let me show you.

50
00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.090
– Ah...!
– Ah...!

51
00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.700
The only thing we guard is this stone.

52
00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.160
Look at that writing.

53
00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.080
What's it mean?

54
00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.420
We don't know.

55
00:04:55.420 --> 00:05:00.260
It is a Poneglyph: writings
left over from ancient history.

56
00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:03.430
You mean this isn't something that
was written by your ancestors?

57
00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:06.900
There is only one
thing we know for sure.

58
00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.400
That the city of Shandora
fought and fell trying

59
00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.840
to protect this stone,
and we will, too.

60
00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.340
As descendants, we feel
it is our duty to continue

61
00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.650
to protect it with the same resolve.

62
00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.780
This stone now represents
proof that our ancestors

63
00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.490
not only fought a
vicious fight, but survived.

64
00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.870
And we revere our ancestors
as we would our gods.

65
00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:33.500
Still, when I heard the bell ringing before,
I had no idea it would be this huge.

66
00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.570
The bell's rings have words to them.

67
00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.980
Words?

68
00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.200
Yes.

69
00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.450
It speaks so that the
spirits of our ancestors

70
00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:49.500
who have passed can still return to this
land at any time without getting lost.

71
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.410
We continue to ring the bell
as if to shout to them,

72
00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:57.260
"We are here!" "Come home!"
"We are waiting for you!"

73
00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:58.640
And the sound.

74
00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:02.480
The sound itself proclaims
the glory of Shandora.

75
00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:06.100
Making its existence known
to the ends of the sea!

76
00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.220
It shouts: "We will never run or hide!"

77
00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:12.890
Because of this, we have
given the grand bell a name.

78
00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.460
We call it the "Fire of Shandora."

79
00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:16.760
Makes sense.

80
00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:19.090
That explains the majestic sound!

81
00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:19.900
You think so?

82
00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:21.440
Yeah!

83
00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.840
It was this fire that reached out
to us and helped us arrive here.

84
00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:31.800
I heard the ringing
during a terrible storm.

85
00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.470
I heard it clearly when it
shouldn't have been audible at all.

86
00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.950
You like the bell's ringing too?

87
00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.580
Yeah, I bet you do.

88
00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.990
I bet someday, you'll grow up
just like that other giant snake.

89
00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.540
But probably not for
another hundred years!

90
00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.710
Noland, I invite you to stay here.

91
00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:01.880
Please.

92
00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:04.490
It's been 400 years
since Shandora fell.

93
00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.660
And you're the first guests we've
had, so I want to welcome you.

94
00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.410
Won't you accept my offer?

95
00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.900
Thank you, Kalgara.

96
00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:15.200
And with your permission I
would also love the opportunity

97
00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.000
to collect some plants from the forest

98
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.870
and see this plague
all the way through.

99
00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.070
Commodore!

100
00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.320
Hold on, now.

101
00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:24.490
What's with the clothes?

102
00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:26.080
We found an Eternal Compass!

103
00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.540
And look at this map, Commodore!

104
00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.160
Just look!

105
00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:32.790
We took these items
from those who intruded upon us.

106
00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.000
Yes.

107
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.750
That skull shape is
definitely our island.

108
00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.760
The name "Shandora" means
"the skull's right eye."

109
00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:43.130
The name refers to the city's location.

110
00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:44.300
Right here.

111
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.910
Well, take care!

112
00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.580
And make sure she
gets plenty of rest, okay?

113
00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.910
I will, thanks! G'bye doctor!

114
00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.730
Hey, look, everyone!

115
00:07:57.730 --> 00:07:59.690
Noland brought us some exotic crops!

116
00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:06.590
I have a greenhouse on our ship
with all kinds of plant samples.

117
00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.840
I'll leave some seeds and sprouts
here that are suited for your soil.

118
00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.720
Does it taste good?

119
00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.640
Very!

120
00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.220
And it's full of nutrients!

121
00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:16.820
All right!

122
00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:19.240
Time to begin another day of hard work!

123
00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.740
Hard work doing what?

124
00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.290
Having a campfire party?

125
00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:30.420
<b>One Month After Landfall</b>

126
00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.670
But why?

127
00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:35.630
Why would the doctor
and the others do this?

128
00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:41.410
Chief!

129
00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:42.740
Noland and the others are coming!

130
00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.490
You are not to say
anything about last night!

131
00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:47.830
Is that clear?

132
00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.790
They said they are going
to set sail in a few days.

133
00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:54.060
So until then, don't do anything rash.

134
00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.560
Do you hear me?

135
00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.940
Fine, then. Our people will
never understand each other.

136
00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:59.690
They've only done harm.

137
00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:01.610
I don't care how good his medicine is.

138
00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.070
He's still a god killer!

139
00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:08.070
Do these people think they can just show
up here and stomp all over our history?

140
00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:09.170
They'll pay!

141
00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:14.580
We must endure it, and we must
wait quietly for them to leave.

142
00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:15.620
They're here!

143
00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:19.960
Hello, everyone.

144
00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.750
I'm looking for Kalgara.

145
00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:32.760
Why is everyone
acting so cold all of a sudden?

146
00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.630
And where's Kalgara?

147
00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:37.500
Turn around and leave now.
You're not welcome.

148
00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.050
You're outsiders.

149
00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:40.860
Kalgara doesn't want
to see you anymore.

150
00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.290
Seto, stop!

151
00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:47.320
When are you going to leave, anyway?

152
00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:48.530
Answer me!

153
00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:52.240
What's going on?

154
00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:54.120
It seems like they suddenly hate us.

155
00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.620
Now, hold on!

156
00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:58.330
You can't just start acting like this!

157
00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.840
It's not fair!

158
00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:00.930
Let it go.

159
00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:04.380
Let's continue our work.

160
00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.730
We still have some forest to inspect.

161
00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:12.990
There you are, Kalgara!

162
00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.120
Noland has been looking for you!

163
00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.450
I know he has.

164
00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.980
I have no desire to speak to him.

165
00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:24.780
If I see him right now,
I'm afraid I might kill him.

166
00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:31.700
That's strange.

167
00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.270
The bell didn't ring today.

168
00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.260
Yeah.

169
00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:36.980
It's the first time that's happened
in the month that we've been here.

170
00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.300
Commodore?

171
00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:43.460
I'll be done exploring
the forest in two days.

172
00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:44.280
Uh... Right.

173
00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.990
Let everyone know
we set sail in three days.

174
00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:51.890
Tell them that this is their last
chance to enjoy dry land for a while.

175
00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:59.290
Commodore, to tell you the truth,
I can't wait to get off this insane island.

176
00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.850
Only after we've finished our duties.

177
00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:02.970
Goodnight.

178
00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.900
You should stay here, Noland!

179
00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:08.240
I have an idea!

180
00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.230
Why don't you make Mousse your wife?

181
00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:12.770
Don't be silly!

182
00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:15.610
I have a family at home
and kids who are her age!

183
00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.200
You're outsiders.

184
00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:21.370
Kalgara doesn't want
to see you anymore.

185
00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:23.630
When are you going to leave, anyway?

186
00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:24.840
Answer me!

187
00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:32.480
I know you're here, Kalgara!

188
00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.570
Come out, now!

189
00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:38.030
I won't understand what's
going on unless you talk to me!

190
00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:39.610
This is ridiculous!

191
00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.160
Not to mention unfair!

192
00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.200
Hey!

193
00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.950
Come on! We set sail in a few days!

194
00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:47.620
I don't want us to part like this!

195
00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:03.890
How dare you show your face here!

196
00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:06.680
Do you want your wife
to live her life as a widow?

197
00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.650
Kalgara!

198
00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.610
The commodore seems sad lately.

199
00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.530
Yeah. It's unfortunate.

200
00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.780
He thought he made such
a good friend out here.

201
00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:30.160
None of this makes any sense.

202
00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:34.170
It looks like we're gonna set
sail first thing tomorrow morning.

203
00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:37.050
The villagers are so upset
that we can't go near them.

204
00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:40.440
Plus, I don't remember ever
hearing the bell ring today.

205
00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.870
How dare you show your face here!

206
00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.790
Do you want your wife to
live her life as a widow?

207
00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:08.990
I gotta say, this is
definitely a tough way to leave.

208
00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:11.500
Doctor?

209
00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.130
Good evening.

210
00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:19.630
Mousse?

211
00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.590
Sorry. May I speak with you?

212
00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:27.610
Idiot!

213
00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.740
Why did I believe he was a botanist?

214
00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:37.720
Damn you, Noland!

215
00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:42.150
If these are the unfortunate
victims of your advancement,

216
00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:46.680
then we never should have accepted
you or trusted you the way we did.

217
00:14:50.270 --> 00:14:52.400
Kindred Trees?

218
00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:54.150
Yes.

219
00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.770
We've been told that
the spirits of our ancestors

220
00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:59.030
who died on this island are guided back

221
00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:02.640
by the sound of a bell so
that they may rest inside them.

222
00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.560
Since the age of Shandora,
every one of our ancestors

223
00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:08.220
who lived on the island
watches over us.

224
00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:12.230
They watch over us from
those sacred, white trees.

225
00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:15.910
That is why the Kindred Wood is
so important to us Shandorians.

226
00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:24.830
That is why we've protected them
as we've protected our own lives.

227
00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:28.620
It's more than just a forest;
it's our history.

228
00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:32.590
Can you see now why
we hold these trees sacred?

229
00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:34.680
And we just chopped them all down.

230
00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.640
The warriors felt so betrayed and angry

231
00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.180
they grabbed their weapons
in search of revenge.

232
00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:42.810
We must drive them off this island!

233
00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.310
– Yeah! All right!
– Yeah! All right!

234
00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:51.640
But because you had already saved so
many lives here, they couldn't just...

235
00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:54.980
I understand.

236
00:15:56.270 --> 00:16:00.020
They were so grateful
that they couldn't act on it.

237
00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:03.730
But Doctor, even if it
was just for tree research.

238
00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.900
Even if you didn't know.

239
00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.740
The villager's anger won't go away.

240
00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.580
So before you go, I thought I'd ask.

241
00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.660
I have to know the reason why.

242
00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:23.270
So their ancestors'
spirits are in those trees?

243
00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:24.940
I can't believe I didn't know.

244
00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:28.440
And now we've done something
terrible that we can't reverse.

245
00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:31.110
They have every right
to be as angry as they are.

246
00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:33.280
But Commodore. We had no choice...

247
00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:35.530
There are no excuses!

248
00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:39.650
I was too wrapped up in my own
interests to even consider theirs.

249
00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:46.240
I was told that besides
proclaiming the city's existence,

250
00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:51.590
the bell also served as a guide for
their ancestors to return to the island.

251
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:55.120
And we just cut them down!

252
00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.950
We do not deserve their forgiveness.

253
00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.580
Commodore, wait.

254
00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:04.420
Listen up, everyone!

255
00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:05.540
– Huh?!
– Huh?!

256
00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:08.180
You want us to leave
the treasure behind?!

257
00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:14.180
I just found out Noland and his
men are getting ready to leave.

258
00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:25.560
Mousse. Where have you been?

259
00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.150
What if...

260
00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:39.330
What if you knew a single
tree was tainted by poison?

261
00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:43.210
Poison that would contaminate the forest,
spreading from tree to tree.

262
00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.300
From tree to people,
and kill the island.

263
00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:49.050
What if you knew about it beforehand?

264
00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:50.830
What are you talking about?

265
00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.440
Please tell us what you mean.

266
00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:53.980
If we had a choice.

267
00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:57.770
What would we do with that one tree?

268
00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.070
What would we do?

269
00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:05.490
Father, listen.

270
00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:06.950
You have to stop them.

271
00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:08.080
You fool.

272
00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.660
Don't you understand what they've done?

273
00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:13.030
We can't leave things this way!
We'll regret it forever!

274
00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.990
You've finally made such a dear friend.

275
00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:18.450
And we owe them so much!

276
00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:21.430
Father, we can't leave
them hurting like this!

277
00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:23.430
What are you talking about?

278
00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:30.420
There is no excuse, but on the
commodore's behalf, I must say this:

279
00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:34.550
Those woods were already dead
before we arrived on this island.

280
00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:38.550
The worst thing about Tree Fever
is that it also infects plant life.

281
00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:43.600
Commodore Noland understood this,
and that was his reason for doing what he did.

282
00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:47.480
This is also why he pleaded with
you without regard for his own life.

283
00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:52.680
From people to forest
and forest to people,

284
00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:59.010
several small islands have been destroyed
in exactly the same way. Killed by fever.

285
00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:03.100
But there's nothing to worry about.

286
00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:07.030
Yesterday, we finished inspecting
the rest of the forest.

287
00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:09.620
I'm sorry we cut down
your forest without knowing.

288
00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.580
And I feel worse that we
never explained why we did it.

289
00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:16.290
It's probably unforgivable
even with an explanation.

290
00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:21.200
But a botanist would never harm
a forest without good reason.

291
00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:24.870
Trust me, the commodore doesn't have
anything against gods or spirits.

292
00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.590
It's just that he
always has to make a choice.

293
00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:33.260
And he always knows
what is most important.

294
00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:36.060
So...

295
00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:38.440
That means that they did all of
that to try to help our people?

296
00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:44.610
Father!

297
00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.420
I'm sorry, Noland!

298
00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.030
Please don't leave yet!

299
00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.880
Does everyone have everything?

300
00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:56.620
Not everything.

301
00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.960
You wuss, hah!

302
00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.540
All right, everyone, to your positions.

303
00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:02.960
It's time to set sail!

304
00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.460
We're now on our way back
to the Lvneel Kingdom!

305
00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.540
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

306
00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:10.610
Noland!

307
00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.310
I can't believe I made such a mistake!

308
00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.230
Noland! Wait!

309
00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.480
Set sail!

310
00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.810
The bell.

311
00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.610
Why would it be ringing now?

312
00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:36.560
– Ring it!

313
00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:38.610
I'm so sorry, Noland!

314
00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:40.820
Ring louder!

315
00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:43.070
Noland and the rest
of them can't hear you!

316
00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:47.660
Look over there!

317
00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.210
Wait! Noland!

318
00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:02.800
Is that you, Kalgara?

319
00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:19.560
Come back!

320
00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.890
Noland!

321
00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.840
Come back, please, Noland!
You've got to!

322
00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.010
I'll ring the bell so you
can find your way back to us!

323
00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:36.680
I don't want you to
lose sight of this island!

324
00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:39.270
Because... one day...

325
00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:42.730
I want you to return, my dear friend.

326
00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:44.500
Noland!

327
00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.290
Please come back!

328
00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:59.970
I know we'll meet
again someday, Noland.

329
00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:01.810
Have a safe voyage.

330
00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:08.110
So... I can come back again?

331
00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:15.520
Of course I will. I'll come back.

332
00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:22.150
Someday, Kalgara!

333
00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:24.650
I know we'll meet
again someday, Noland.

334
00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:40.500
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

335
00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:45.920
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

336
00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:48.720
You are so much like the moon

337
00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:53.370
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

338
00:22:56.820 --> 00:23:05.770
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

339
00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:11.000
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

340
00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:19.310
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

341
00:23:19.950 --> 00:23:26.200
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

342
00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:31.820
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

343
00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:37.590
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

344
00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:43.980
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
